Generally, no. According to the council's guidance, a garden shed under 2.5 metres high, sited behind the front wall of the house and covering less than half the garden, does not usually need a planning application.

A few things could change that:

- **Conservation areas and listed buildings** have different rules, so an application may be needed even for a small shed.
- **Location and size**: if the shed would be in front of the house or cover half or more of the garden, check before building.

If you tell me your address, I can check whether it has any planning constraints, such as a conservation area or listed building status. This is general guidance only, not a formal planning opinion. If you're unsure, the council can confirm whether your specific plans need an application.
